    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector",
    "problem": "Find $\\text{Re}(k)$ given that\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\overset{―}{kv}=[\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$",
    "worked_solution": "Since $\\overset{―}{kv}=\\overset{―}{v},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ (-5+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4\\overset{―}{k}=-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ (-5+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}=18-40\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{k}=-5+7\\text{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain the true statement\n\n$$\n(-5+\\text{i})(-5+7\\text{i})=18-40\\text{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{―}{-5+7\\text{i}}=-5-7\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Re}(k)=-5.$",
